  "deletedAt": null,
  "deletedBy": null,
  "details": "# Issue:\n\nWhen using a relatively tall Avatar that is above the max 5m, it wont really work with the new Avatar Scale system.\n\nThe Avatar works fine for the most part, but once you use the scale system you are going to be limited to the 5max until you reset your Avatar. \n\n# Expected Behavior / Suggesion:  \n\nI'm honestly not sure on what the best behavior would be here, but I have 3 ideas:  \n\n1. Limit the height to 5m once they load into the Avatar.\n\n- This would result in the limiting system actually doing it's job  \n\n- It would kinda break / limit people with tall Avatars though\n\n2. Set the max height to the Avatars default height if it's above the 5m limit\n\n- people would still be able to have big Avatars this way  \n\n-  it would kinda defeat the point of a 5m max system\n\n3. Make the system scale factor instead of view height based  \n\n- people could always scale up / down their Avatar no matter who tall it was originally  \n\n- it would be really hard to implement height limits this way",
  "error": null,
